                <pb facs="0623" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg539"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Law fixing dues for sanitary visits of September</hi>
                    22, 1874.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. A visit due, of which half remains in
                    the public treasury, and the other half is to be paid directly to the doctors,
                    named in the different ports of the Republic to examine the crews and to oversee
                    the execution of the regulations coming from the secretary of state of interior,
                    is established as follows: <table cols="2" rend="width: 80%;"
                        rendition="#center" rows="5">
                        <row>
                            <cell>For all vessel of—</cell>
                            <cell/>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell role="num">301 tons and over</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$16 00</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell role="num">201 tons to 300</cell>
                            <cell role="num">12 00</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell role="num">200 tons and under</cell>
                            <cell role="num">8 00</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell role="num">For each steamer of whatever tonnage</cell>
                            <cell role="num">25 00</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
            </div>
        </body>
